# TSX types and utils

Hard project conventions for every `.tsx` change. Do not skip.

## 1. Types out of TSX when > 5 lines

- Count pure TypeScript type blocks in the file (`type`, `interface`, complex unions/mapped types). Simple props of a few lines may stay inline.
- If total type-declaration lines are **greater than 5**, move them to a dedicated types file and import into the TSX.
- File locations:
  - One component/page: co-located `ComponentName.types.ts` (e.g. `LoginForm.types.ts`)
  - Shared inside a feature: `features/<name>/types/` with `index.ts` barrel
  - Shared across the app: `shared/types/` with `index.ts` barrel

## 2. No helper functions in TSX

- Never put support/helpers (format, parse, map, validate, transform, etc.) in `.tsx` files.
- UI event handlers that only wire props/hooks (`handleSubmit`) may stay in the component; pure logic goes to utils.
- Utils locations:
  - Feature-only: `features/<name>/utils/` with `index.ts` barrel
  - Cross-feature: `shared/utils/` with `index.ts` barrel

### Before adding any new helper

1. Search the whole repo (code-review-graph and/or Grep / semantic search) for a similar function.
2. If an existing helper is roughly **≥ 70%** the same purpose/behavior, **stop**. Ask the user whether to refactor it into a shared util for the whole app.
3. Only add a new helper after the user answers, or when no close match exists.
